ip6-nd: learn from a neighbor solicitation only after validating it

The NS/NA node learned the sender's MAC before checking the NS target, so
any NS that was later dropped (target not owned by this interface) still
created or updated a neighbor entry. NAs are learned as before; NSs are
learned only once the target has been found. The link-local FIB lookup
also no longer uses an unset per-interface link-local table (~0).

Part of the VPP source used for the RK3588 board build (v26.06-1-geth1test); the
RK3588 board's libvnet links the ip6_nd object built from it.

--- a/src/vnet/ip6-nd/ip6_nd.c
+++ b/src/vnet/ip6-nd/ip6_nd.c
@@ -39,6 +39,21 @@
 static ip6_link_delegate_id_t ip6_nd_delegate_id;
 static ip6_nd_t *ip6_nd_pool;
 
+static_always_inline void
+ip6_nd_learn (u32 sw_if_index, const ip6_address_t *ip, const u8 *ethernet_address)
+{
+  ip_neighbor_learn_t learn = {
+    .sw_if_index = sw_if_index,
+    .ip = {
+      .version = AF_IP6,
+      .ip.ip6 = *ip,
+    },
+  };
+
+  mac_address_from_bytes (&learn.mac, ethernet_address);
+  ip_neighbor_learn_dp (&learn);
+}
